WEBVTT

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:09.960
Mai, I didn't know you were in such pain.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:14.900
But it's wrong to risk our lives in this kind of duel!

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:16.920
I've made up my mind!

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.440
I'll fight you with all my might!

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:26.040
And Mai, I promise to find a way to save us both!

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:48.070
Before I knew it, I abandoned happiness to survive

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:55.210
Lying to myself, I danced clinging on to illusions

00:00:55.990 --> 00:01:01.870
At the edge of my vision when I close my eyes

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:07.860
I was searching for your smile

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:15.230
With our memories fading

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:22.310
We hold on to our dreams and run  Yeah

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:29.210
These feelings that I shut away in my heart

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:36.440
I'll now grasp them again

00:01:55.060 --> 00:02:01.070
Resurrect!  The Third Dragon

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:17.140
C'mon!  If Jonouchi doesn't do something this turn, he'll lose!

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:19.800
The loser will lose their soul.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:22.820
I don't want that happening to either of them!

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:29.390
My other self, there's really nothing we can do?

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:35.830
The Seal of Orichalcos won't vanish until one of them loses all their life points.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:39.280
But that's the key to saving them.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:42.530
If Jonouchi realizes that...

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:44.350
You mean...

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.830
It's pointless to keep fighting.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:51.160
One final strike and Jonouchi's soul will belong to Doma.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:52.350
Right, Rafael?

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.090
What's wrong?

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:57.440
Nothing.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:05.630
I only have 200 life points while Mai still has 4000.

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:08.370
She has more monsters as well.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:11.960
But I can't give up.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:15.870
As long as I have a card in my deck, I still have a chance.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:19.390
There must be a way to save us both.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:22.880
If only I can destroy this seal...

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:25.370
Wait a sec!  Maybe...

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:29.890
I have to try this!  I'll bet on this card!

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:35.680
I summon The Fiend Megacyber in attack position!

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.660
Megacyber?

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:43.930
It's a Level 6 monster, but if you have at least two more monsters than me...

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:46.440
...I can Special Summon it without tributing!

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:52.900
The Fiend Megacyber attacks Harpie Lady!

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:03.650
Nice!  He started his counterattack!

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:08.060
But is Jonouchi really going to fight Mai?

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.810
No.  Jonouchi realized something.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.670
He realized how to end this duel.

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:21.420
If their life points reach 0 simultaneously, the seal may vanish.

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:24.680
He must've realized that opportunity.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:28.580
Jonouchi suddenly wants to duel.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:31.920
He is a chosen duelist after all.

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:35.920
But Mai is still going to win.

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.820
I set a card!

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:40.560
I end my turn!

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.770
About time you started playing seriously.

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:46.570
Yeah.  Super serious!

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:51.300
Good.  This is what I was waiting for!

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:56.420
Fighting you when you're serious without your lame friendship!

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.580
And I will win!

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:03.040
Where am I?

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:07.750
Don't worry.  Your wishes will come true here.

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:11.840
What will you do to me?

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:14.440
Welcome, Mai Kujaku.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:17.090
Welcome to Doma's temple.

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:19.600
Who are you?

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:21.680
I am Dartz.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:25.100
I'll make your wishes come true.

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.610
My wishes?

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:30.340
The fear in your heart...

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:35.850
The fear of despair and loneliness after losing...

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:42.320
I'm the only one who can free you of that fear.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.850
That's nonsense!

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:47.360
I...  I...

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:49.860
I'm not afraid of anything!

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:52.880
I'm not afraid...

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:58.430
Go, The Winged Dragon of Ra!

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:00.300
God Blaze Cannon!

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:08.650
Mai Kujaku, enjoy the world of pain that's inside your heart!

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.400
No...

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.320
I don't want to lose!

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:32.140
I don't want to feel that way again!

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.510
Then keep winning.

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:42.510
Those who were kind to you have moved ahead and left you behind.

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:47.200
Will you keep wandering in a maze alone?

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:51.740
Or will you catch up and surpass them?

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:53.440
You choose.

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:56.960
Don't you want to win, Mai Kujaku?

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:00.060
I want to win.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:03.470
Are you willing to give up everything?

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:05.470
I want to win.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.810
I want to win at any cost!

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:13.810
Want the power to achieve that?

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:15.130
I do!

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:17.180
Then I'll give it to you.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:34.600
You've now joined Doma.

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:37.300
My turn!  I draw!

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:41.540
With all my strength, Jonouchi...

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:43.330
I will defeat you!

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:51.690
Your driving is insane.

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:55.360
Something's wrong.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.460
Why is no one here?

00:07:58.150 --> 00:08:01.460
Wait!  Don't leave us behind!

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:05.800
Yugi!  Everyone!

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:07.200
Otogi!

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.090
Otogi?

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:12.240
What are you doing here?

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:16.040
Why are you dueling here?

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:19.780
Is Jonouchi dueling... Mai?

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:22.270
There's no time to explain!

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:24.170
It's a mess!

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:26.080
We're trapped in here.

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:28.020
Can you open it from the outside?

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:30.260
Okay!  I'll try!

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:31.760
Thanks, Otogi!

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:36.590
Huh?  Ryuzaki and Haga?

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:38.500
Why are you also here?

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:40.100
Well, uh...

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:43.830
That's the seal we saw before!

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:48.110
Yeah!  We couldn't do anything against it!

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:53.320
I tribute two Harpie Lady copies.

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:56.390
I summon Harpie's Pet Dragon!

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:03.850
The Seal of Orichalcos's effect gives it 500 attack points!

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:09.460
And it gains 300 attack points for every Harpie Lady on the field!

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:14.360
3400 attack points?

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:19.800
She's fired up!  She's totally different than during Duelist Kingdom!

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:23.980
Why does Mai Kujaku have that Seal card?

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.580
It's over, Jonouchi!

00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:29.480
Go, Harpie's Pet Dragon!

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:31.710
Attack Megacyber!

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:36.080
I flip over my set card!

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:37.580
Compensation Mediation!

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:42.680
Shuffle this card with two cards of your choosing in your graveyard.

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:48.360
If I manage to draw this card, this turn's battle ends!

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:54.250
What?  He only has a 1-in-3 chance of drawing his card!

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:56.430
If he picks wrong, he loses!

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:58.330
His last gasp.

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:05.610
Actually, if he has the heart of a true duelist, he may be able to draw it.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:10.920
Choose two cards from your graveyard, Mai!

00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:14.860
These two.

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:18.560
Okay.  You shuffle.

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:34.540
Well...

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:36.540
I'm ready.

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:43.550
Here I go.

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:49.560
I choose that card!

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:06.400
I choose that card!

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:26.090
Yeah!

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:29.610
Oh yeah!  He did it!

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:30.700
Hooray!

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:32.040
No way!

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:34.700
He's always lucky.

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:37.210
He actually did it.

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:39.710
This turn's battle ends!

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:47.950
Good.  He managed to survive this turn.

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:50.950
But he'll pay a big price.

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:52.440
Impressive.

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:55.890
Your instincts are commendable.  But...

00:11:57.770 --> 00:11:59.850
Yeah, I know.

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:05.370
Since I picked correctly, you can put the cards you chose on top of your deck.

00:12:07.230 --> 00:12:10.870
What?  She can use those cards again?

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:15.610
Both Phoenix Formation and Sparrow Formation are powerful cards.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:19.610
Mai will get one of them on her next draw.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:23.680
The battle may be over, but my turn isn't!

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:28.320
Due to The Seal of Orichalcos's effect, I move Harpie Lady to the rear!

00:12:29.550 --> 00:12:32.360
Then I set two cards!

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:33.840
I end my turn!

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:41.670
I survived this time, but my Megacyber won't be enough for her next attack.

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:47.370
And if Mai draws Phoenix Formation next turn, I'm finished.

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:49.880
But there's still a chance!

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:51.880
My turn!  I draw!

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:54.380
I set a card!

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:58.020
And I summon a monster in facedown defense position!

00:12:58.280 --> 00:13:00.980
I also switch Megacyber to defense position!

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:05.160
Hey, only focusing on defense again?

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:07.140
Be quiet!

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:12.970
Also locked!

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:16.470
No good!

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:20.810
I have to hurry!

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:24.060
Damn!  Locked!

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:25.580
No!

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:28.580
It opened!

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:37.990
You're calm despite being in trouble, Jonouchi.

00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:44.530
I guess.  I learned in Battle City to never give up.

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:47.000
And I'll get another chance.

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:51.900
That's right.  Back then, I was waiting to be saved.

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:53.720
That's why I must win now!

00:13:54.030 --> 00:13:56.020
My turn!  I draw!

00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:58.010
I flip over my set card!

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:00.020
Drop Off!

00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:02.020
I won't let you draw!

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:06.270
I don't think so!  I also flip over a set card!

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:08.360
Trap Jammer!

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:13.860
By discarding one card, your trap card's activation is negated!

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:18.240
Oh no!

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:20.370
What did Mai draw?

00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:24.350
You're really lucky.

00:14:24.350 --> 00:14:25.870
I'll set this.

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:29.880
That card is Sparrow Formation, not Phoenix Formation!

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:32.320
But you're not safe yet!

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:35.900
Harpie's Pet Dragon attacks Megacyber!

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:46.460
Harpie Lady attacks your facedown defense monster!

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:55.380
All right!  Fiber Jar's Flip Effect activates!

00:14:55.380 --> 00:15:02.110
We return our hands, graveyards and monsters on our fields to our decks and reshuffle!

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.520
Well done, Jonouchi.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.860
But it won't work!

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:08.740
I flip over my set card!

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:10.620
Harpie's Feather Storm!

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:19.680
My Harpie's attack activates this card's effect!

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:22.760
Your monster's effects are negated!

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:30.640
Jonouchi's monsters are all destroyed again!

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:31.610
Jonouchi...

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:36.110
Mai read all of Jonouchi's moves.  She's tough!

00:15:36.110 --> 00:15:37.950
I end my turn.

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:41.120
What will you try next, Jonouchi?

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:44.540
It's not over yet!  I still have life points!

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:47.350
My turn!  I draw!

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:52.130
I summon a monster in facedown defense position!

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:54.240
I end my turn!

00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:59.600
Mai will draw Phoenix Formation next turn.

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:03.720
No matter what monster he has, he only has 200 life points.  It's over.

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:05.470
My turn!  I draw!

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:10.480
Jonouchi has one monster on his field.

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:14.710
If my Harpies attack together, I win.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:21.370
But what if his facedown monster has an effect, like Fiber Jar?

00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:27.460
I'll use Phoenix Formation's effect to negate its effects and destroy it!

00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:30.460
I activate a spell card from my hand!

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:31.890
Phoenix Formation!

00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:34.080
Your facedown monster is destroyed!

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:36.250
I win!

00:16:57.020 --> 00:16:57.990
Good!

00:16:57.990 --> 00:16:59.740
Jonouchi...

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:11.540
Neko Mane King?

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:16.300
Yeah.  Neko Mane King has 0 attack points.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:23.560
Phoenix Formation subtracts the destroyed monster's attack points from my life points.  So it's pointless.

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:31.040
Then I activate Neko Mane King's effect!

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:38.560
If a spell, trap or monster effect sends it to the graveyard during your turn, your turn ends!

00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:41.610
Thank goodness!

00:17:41.610 --> 00:17:44.150
He survived.  Barely.

00:17:44.150 --> 00:17:46.810
How lucky can he get?

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:49.290
He doesn't know when to give up.

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:52.310
He only delayed his defeat by a turn.

00:17:52.310 --> 00:17:53.840
I've had enough!

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:57.920
Don't you dare think you can still save me!

00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:02.800
Sorry, but you know I don't give up.

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:06.340
But Mai's impressive.

00:18:06.340 --> 00:18:08.960
She won't let me wait for an opening.

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:13.960
If I can't do something after my next draw, I'll lose.

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:17.770
Will it really end like this?

00:18:17.770 --> 00:18:22.940
I can't save Mai or defeat Doma?

00:18:23.260 --> 00:18:25.680
No, it won't end like this!

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:27.450
I won't give up!

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:30.450
Please, my deck.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:32.910
I don't care if it's a miracle.

00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:34.880
Just give me a chance!

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:42.430
What?

00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:48.170
Eye of Timaeus is...

00:18:48.170 --> 00:18:49.440
Can it be?

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:00.180
What's this glow?

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:04.890
Fang of Critias!  This is the same as before!

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:21.090
Where are we?  Where's Mai?

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:23.040
What happened to our duel?

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:27.250
This is the world of Duel Monsters, where nameless dragons sleep.

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:32.210
This sword...

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:35.520
Jonouchi, draw that sword.

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:36.210
What?

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:38.960
Only you can draw it.

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:42.440
You're the last one chosen by the nameless dragon.

00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:43.870
Me?

00:19:55.900 --> 00:20:01.010
I can feel someone speaking to me through the sword.

00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:18.750
Nameless dragon, I know your name!

00:20:20.140 --> 00:20:22.490
Your name is Hermos!

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:33.140
Was that a dream?

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:34.070
No.

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:36.580
That's right, Jonouchi.

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:39.580
You were chosen by the nameless dragon.

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:43.080
What was that?

00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:45.640
What's wrong, big brother?

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:48.690
Mokuba, you didn't see the light?

00:20:48.690 --> 00:20:50.520
Huh?  What do you mean?

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:52.540
Never mind.

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:56.590
The Orichalcos is reacting!

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:58.860
Is it the nameless dragon's power?

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:02.110
Interfering again?

00:21:02.640 --> 00:21:05.100
What happened?

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:08.460
What are you doing?  It's your turn!

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:13.110
I don't know what it is, but I feel a power inside me.

00:21:13.740 --> 00:21:16.120
I'll bet it all on this card!

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:17.020
I draw!

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:19.620
This is...

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:21.790
Claw of Hermos!

00:21:22.320 --> 00:21:26.680
What's with Jonouchi?  He's acting weird.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:27.630
Yeah.

00:21:28.140 --> 00:21:32.170
I knew Jonouchi was the final chosen one!

00:21:32.170 --> 00:21:34.630
Yeah.  With that card...

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:42.140
Please, Hermos!  Lend me your strength!

00:21:57.100 --> 00:22:06.010
The streets flow by, colored in red

00:22:06.510 --> 00:22:14.350
If you notice your pain, it changes to joy

00:22:16.080 --> 00:22:25.510
People learn of friendship every time they wipe their tears

00:22:26.130 --> 00:22:35.030
With the warm strength you gave me, I'll change them into kindness

00:22:35.600 --> 00:22:44.060
My overflowing emotions don't stop

00:22:44.840 --> 00:22:49.570
I'll live feeling them

00:22:50.180 --> 00:22:54.750
For me to be me

00:22:54.750 --> 00:23:03.210
Overflowing friendship heals me

00:23:03.890 --> 00:23:08.850
Our chance meeting was real

00:23:09.370 --> 00:23:18.510
We'll both understand that someday

00:23:24.940 --> 00:23:30.820
Jonouchi is in a total pinch when he gets a card.  What is it?

00:23:30.820 --> 00:23:35.450
Just like how Yugi got a legendary dragon card in the world of Duel Monsters...

00:23:35.450 --> 00:23:39.000
...Jonouchi was also chosen by a card!

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:41.580
The nameless dragon, Claw of Hermos.

00:23:41.580 --> 00:23:47.020
Can that card's power save Jonouchi and Mai?

00:23:47.320 --> 00:23:49.620
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Hermos's Miracle

00:23:49.620 --> 00:23:51.200
Duel, standby!
